{id:'group',level:'B1',title:'A change of plan',minutes:7,text:'Hello everyone. Our study group this Saturday will meet at Riverside Cafe because the central library meeting room is being repaired. Please arrive at ten fifteen so we can start at ten thirty. Bring a notebook and the article I sent. You can read it on your phone; printing is unnecessary. The session is free, but you pay for your own drink.',questions:[q('Where will the group meet?',['Central library','Riverside Cafe','At school'],1,'The library room is under repair.'),q('When should people arrive?',['10:00','10:15','10:30'],1,'Arrival is 10:15; start is 10:30.'),q('Printing the article is required.',['True','False','Not given'],1,'Reading on a phone is fine.')]},
{id:'survey',level:'B2',title:'Research meeting',minutes:9,text:'We originally intended to interview forty commuters, but we reduced the sample to twenty-four so each interview could be longer. The first eight interviews took place online. We then moved to face-to-face meetings because participants gave fuller answers. This does not prove online interviews are always less useful. Our revised report must explain the change and acknowledge that the two groups may differ in other ways.',questions:[q('What was the final sample size?',null,'twenty-four','The sample was reduced to twenty-four.'),q('Why change interview format?',['To obtain fuller responses','To reduce travel','To remove the report'],0,'Participants gave fuller answers face to face.'),q('Online interviews are always inferior.',['True','False','Not given'],1,'The speaker explicitly rejects this generalisation.')]},
{id:'policy',level:'C1',title:'Interpreting a pilot project',minutes:10,text:'The pilot’s headline figures are encouraging, but we should resist extrapolating them to the whole city. Participation was voluntary, which means the sample may overrepresent residents already interested in public transport. Moreover, the subsidy coincided with roadworks that made driving unusually inconvenient. Before expanding the scheme, we propose a phased rollout with independent evaluation, allowing us to distinguish lasting changes from temporary responses.',questions:[q('What threatens representativeness?',['Voluntary participation','Independent evaluation','A phased rollout'],0,'Volunteers may already be unusually interested.'),q('What coincided with the subsidy?',null,'roadworks','Roadworks made driving inconvenient.'),q('What is the speaker’s attitude?',['Unqualified enthusiasm','Cautious optimism','Complete rejection'],1,'Promising results are acknowledged, but stronger evaluation is requested.')]}
